1. WHAT YOU MAY DO

   Any person or company, including competitors of Astronauta Martech,
   may, free of charge:

   a) use, copy, install and adapt the Material for their own use or
      their organization's use;
   b) use the Material, original or adapted, to provide services to
      third parties and charge for those services, for example as an
      agency, consultancy or freelancer;
   c) install the Material, original or adapted, in a client's tools or
      accounts as part of a service provided to that client;
   d) share the Material free of charge, original or adapted, subject
      to clause 3;
   e) freely use, including commercially, whatever the skills produce
      in your use (specifications, reports, diagnostics, assembled
      workflows and training materials), as long as that output does
      not reproduce a substantial part of the Material.

2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

   You may not charge for the Material itself. You may not, directly
   or indirectly:

   a) sell, resell, rent or sublicense the Material, original or
      adapted;
   b) include the Material, in whole or in substantial part, in a paid
      product, such as a course, paid training, template pack,
      subscription, marketplace, plugin store or commercial software;
   c) offer access to the Material in exchange for payment.

   In short: charging for work done with the Material is allowed;
   charging for the Material is not.

3. ATTRIBUTION

   Every copy or adaptation, in whole or in part, must keep this
   license notice and credit "Astronauta Martech" as the author of the
   original Material.

4. NO WARRANTY

   The Material is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind.
   Astronauta Martech is not liable for any damage, loss or effect
   arising from the use of the Material, including changes to
   accounts, workflows, leads or third-party data. Users are
   responsible for what they execute with it.

5. TRADEMARKS

   This license grants no right to use the Astronauta Martech or
   Astronauta Digital trademarks, nor third-party trademarks mentioned
   in the Material, such as Claude, Anthropic, Codex and OpenAI, which
   belong to their respective owners. Names of services and connectors
   displayed by the software while it runs belong to their respective
   owners and appear only to identify the service in use, without
   implying affiliation, sponsorship or endorsement.

6. TERMINATION

   Any breach of this license automatically terminates the rights
   granted to the party in breach.

7. GOVERNING LAW AND VENUE

   This license is governed by the laws of the Federative Republic of
   Brazil. The courts of the judicial district of the head office of
   Astronauta Digital LTDA shall have jurisdiction over any dispute
